Backport of vllm-project/vllm#64059 (merged 2026-11-04, merge commit
d3a3230931f3815f3d2e06ff93caf10055f453ba) to vLLM **0.32.0**, which fixes
#63587.

Upstream's patch does not apply to 0.32.0: the refactor of
`autoregressive/speculator.py` and the tail of `speculator.py` moved between
0.32.0 and the 0.32.1 dev branch. Two hunks are needed instead of three; the
`map_to_kernel_block_table` API itself does exist in 0.32.0
(`vllm/v1/worker/utils.py`, `target_dependent_ar/speculator.py`), so this is a
faithful backport, not a reimplementation.

What it fixes: with the default FULL_AND_PIECEWISE cudagraph mode, the DFlash
draft replayed a FULL graph without refreshing its kernel block table, so on a
hybrid GDN target it read stale KV blocks and almost no draft token was
accepted (0.004 acceptance, ~3.7x slower).

Apply inside the vLLM 0.32.0 container, from the directory that contains the
`vllm/` package (for the official image that is
/usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages):

    patch -p1 --dry-run < vllm-0320-dflash-kernel-block-table.patch
    patch -p1 < vllm-0320-dflash-kernel-block-table.patch

or, for a derived image:

    FROM vllm/vllm-openai:v0.32.0
    COPY vllm-0320-dflash-kernel-block-table.patch /tmp/
    RUN cd /usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages && \
        patch -p1 < /tmp/vllm-0320-dflash-kernel-block-table.patch

Verified against the v0.32.0 tag source: both hunks apply, both files parse.
Runtime behaviour (acceptance > 0.3) is not verified here; it needs a GPU.

Scope: the backported fix addresses the split kernel-block-table path, which
FlashAttention v4 hd256 selects on Blackwell. On Hopper/Ada the tables are not
split, so if acceptance stays 0 with this patch, look at #58894 (prefix caching)
instead.

--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/speculator.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/speculator.py
@@ -599,3 +599,11 @@
         for groups in self.attn_groups:
             for group in groups:
                 group.update_draft_decode_metadata(attn_metadata)
+
+    def _map_kernel_block_tables(self) -> None:
+        """Refresh the persistent kernel block tables a FULL graph reads."""
+        for groups in self.attn_groups:
+            for group in groups:
+                group.map_to_kernel_block_table(
+                    self.block_tables.input_block_tables[group.kv_cache_group_id]
+                )
--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash/speculator.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash/speculator.py
@@ -505,6 +505,8 @@
                 step=self.num_query_per_req,
                 causal=self._group_causal,
             )
+        else:
+            self._map_kernel_block_tables()
 
         # DFlash processes all speculative tokens in one forward pass,
         # so the real token count is num_query_tokens.
